Hi Janet,

Ahead of our 9:30 a.m. Denver discussion on April 17, I've attached the slide=
 overview and the purchasing comparison separately. The current term ends Apr=
il 30, so the overview also sets out a short extension for continuity while w=
e work through the annual terms.

The 520-seat option is USD 248,000 annually, with 60 hours of support and USD=
 2,000 of room under your USD 250,000 annual ceiling. Could you think about w=
hich work JDH would want those 60 hours to cover? We should also discuss the =
conditions for a migration start before settling the scope. The 560-seat opti=
on is USD 266,000 annually, USD 16,000 over the ceiling; the 480-seat option =
is USD 238,000 with support comparable to your current scope.

The proposed three-month extension for the existing 480 seats is a separate a=
greement for USD 58,000, not part of any of the annual prices. We can discuss=
 the coverage period on Friday.

Thanks,
Michelle

